WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.940
We were looking at the TV.

2
00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:02.500
They were saying about the storm was coming.

3
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:06.980
And we would say, okay, we're going to get ready in case we had to get out, you know.

4
00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:13.180
I'd say the day before, we had went and got some canned goods and stuff and got . . . you know, just got things ready.

5
00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:18.880
I said, "Well, I'm going to go to work and we'll see what's going to happen from then."

6
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:30.356
About nine o'clock I went to the door and I looked out, I said, "The street is mighty glassy."

7
00:00:30.356 --> 00:00:30.920
And my momma, she came and she looked.

8
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:33.140
I said, "That's water out there."

9
00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:36.760
I said, "Well, oh, that water's going to go down."

10
00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.900
So then the [?] start getting worse, you know?

11
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.720
So I called my husband at work, I said, "Look you better come on home," I said, "because I don't know what's going to happen."

12
00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:45.140
So he came home.

13
00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:52.020
At about eleven o'clock I looked outside; that water was at the first step.

14
00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:57.880
I said "Y'all," I said, "don't look like we're going anywhere."

15
00:00:57.880 --> 00:00:59.720
I said, "Look like it's coming up."

16
00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:02.420
I said, "Well it might just be a little bit of a flooding."

17
00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:07.290
So about twelve o'clock one of the kids yelled, "Momma!

18
00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:08.860
Water's coming up in the house!

19
00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:09.740
Water's coming in the house!"

20
00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:10.800
I said, "Oh Lord!"

21
00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.920
So we just started running around like somebody crazy.

22
00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:18.640
So the water got up and started coming up and up so we went next door.

23
00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:23.180
The kids, we put them on a mattress and they were floating around.

24
00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:25.300
Now, they thought it was fun.

25
00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:32.320
I had four old people, my momma and my three cousins over there.

26
00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:34.520
I had four children.

27
00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:36.000
None of us could swim.

28
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.960
I said "Lord, I cannot drink all this water.

29
00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:40.480
How am I going to get out of here?"

30
00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:43.960
My husband said, "Look, just be calm."

31
00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:45.440
He said, "We're going to get out of here."

32
00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:46.920
I said, "Okay."

33
00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:50.560
We stayed in that water until one o'clock the next day.

34
00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:55.020
But what happened was the helicopters started passing.

35
00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:58.240
We got out there with white handkerchiefs and started waving, telling them, "We need help!

36
00:01:58.240 --> 00:01:59.120
We need help!"

37
00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:01.400
So the guys from the yacht club came in.

38
00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.580
Like I said, we left out of here, the water was up to here.

39
00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:08.020
When the water settled, it settled halfway up the walls.

40
00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:17.080
And we couldn't come down here until . . . like about two weeks before we could come in the area to see what we could do.

41
00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:18.660
It was just devastated.

42
00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:20.700
We lost everything because everything was water soaked.

43
00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:27.760
Well, after we washed the house out, we stayed away for about a month to let everything just dry out.

44
00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:31.940
I promised the Lord, I said, "Lord if you get me out of here,

45
00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:35.380
you ain't going to have no trouble with me going to church and doing what I'm supposed to do!"

46
00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:36.500
And I kept my promise.
